TITLE:: SLiCE
summary:: Simple Live Coding Environment
categories:: Live Coding, Patterns
related:: Classes/Event, Classes/Pattern, Classes/Pbind, Classes/Pdef

DESCRIPTION::
SLiCE is a Simple Live Coding Environment, that provides a simplified framework for pattern interaction by adding useful default values and a streamlined link::Classes/SynthDef:: factory. It adds default values to link::Classes/Event::'s \note type; i.e., do not change the \type in the patterns you write within SLiCE.

The main difference to working with regular patterns and events is the added \sound key, that automatically sets other necessary event keys for various types of instruments. From a user perspective, one does not have think about whether the sound is a sample, a synth function, or an external MIDI instrument (although the latter is not yet implemented). Furthermore, everything is wrapped within a link::Classes/SynthDef:: providing waveshaping, beat-synced delay, resonant highpass and lowpass filters, beat-synced vibrato (FM) and tremolo (AM), saturation, and an auxiliary output for sending to a reverb in the master synth. All values are clipped to stay within sane ranges and to avoid unintended sonic explosions. The master synth also contains a link::Classes/Limiter:: to further protect your ears.


SUBSECTION:: Discussion
The available default synth parameters and ranges are listed below. Usage depends of the synth, but they are listed here in the processing order. Note that any parameter you add to synth functions using the addSound method will also be available for use in patterns.
code::
\loop // loop a sample (0 or 1)
\vibrato // vibrato amount (bipolar deviation from base frequency in Hz)
\vibratoRate // vibrato rate in number of beats
\fmFreq // frequency modulation frequency in Hz
\fmAmt // frequency modulation amount (bipolar deviation from base frequency in Hz)
\tremolo // tremolo amount (0 - 1)
\tremoloRate // tremolo rate in number of beats
\shaper // waveshaper amount (0 - 1)
\shaperBufA // waveshape for waveshaper buffer A (Integer values 0 - inf (the value is wrapped to the number of available buffers))
\shaperBufB // waveshape for waveshaper buffer B (Integer values 0 - inf (the value is wrapped to the number of available buffers))
\shaperMorph // morph between waveshaper buffer A and B (-1.0 - 1.0)
\shaperWarp // the signal sent into the waveshapers (1.0 - 20.0)
\pan // stereo panning (-1.0 - 1.0)
\hpf // hipass filter frequency (20 - 20000 Hz)
\hpr // hipass filter resonance (0.001 - 0.999)
\lpf // lopass filter frequency (20 - 20000 Hz)
\lpr // lopass filter resonance (0.001 - 0.999)
\delay // delay mix (0 - 1)
\delTime // delay time in number of beats (0.001 - 4.0)
\delFbTime // delay feedback time in number of beats (0- inf)
\saturation // tanh distortion (1 - 99)
\atk // the attack time of the amplitude envelope (seconds)
\rel // the attack time of the amplitude envelope (seconds)
\amp // amplitude (0 - 1)
\reverb // reverb aux post send (0 - 1)
::

SUBSUBSECTION:: The Master
All synths generated by patterns will be passed through a master synth containing reverb (an link::Classes/NHHall::), saturation by tanh, and a link::Classes/Limiter::. See below for examples of how to set parameters for the master synth. The available parameters for the link::Classes/NHHall:: reverb are:
code::
\revTime // decay (0.0 - inf)
\revStereo // stereo spread rate (0.0 - 1.0)
\revLoFreq // low freq cutoff (20 - 20000 Hz)
\revLoRatio // decay rate multiplier for low frequencies (0.0 - 1.0)
\revHiFreq // hi freq cutoff (20 - 20000 Hz)
\revHiRatio // decay rate multiplier for high frequencies (0.0 - 1.0)
\revEarlyDiffusion // early reflections (0.0 - 1.0)
\revLateDiffusion // late reflections (0.0 -1.0)
\revModRate // modulation rate for late reflections (0.0 - 1.0)
\revModDepth // modulation depth for late reflections (0.0 - 1.0)
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: pathToSounds
By default SLiCE looks for a folder called "sounds" in the root of its directory. You can use this argument to point to a different folder if needed.

METHOD:: synthFuncs
Stores some basic synth functions for sample playback and simple waveforms. This method is not intended for direct user interaction, but it is of course possible to add your own functions to the class file here if you want. However, the idea is to keep the basics at a minimal, and instead promote the use of the addSound method for the addition of new synth functions.

SUBSUBSECTION:: Discussion
The available default synth functions are:
code::
\sine, \saw, \pulse, \triangle, \whiteNoise, \pinkNoise, \brownNoise
::
There are also two synth functions for playing mono or stereo samples. These are selected automatically whenever the pattern event's \sound key refers to a sample buffer.

METHOD:: buildSynthDefs
Private method for building a link::Classes/SynthDef:: using link::Classes/SynthDef::.wrap. Can be used directly, but it is preferable to use the .addSound method to add new synthdef functions instead.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: addSound
Use this method to add single soundfiles, a folder of soundfiles, a synth function, or a link::Classes/MIDIEndPoint::.
argument:: name
Give the sound a unique name (a symbol) to be used in the pattern. If the sound is a soundfile and the name is nil, the file name will be used. In the case of a synth function or a link::Classes/MIDIEndPoint::, the name cannot be nil.
argument:: sound
The sound can be a path to a single soundfile, a path to a folder of soundfiles, an ugenGraphFunc to be wrapped into the main link::Classes/SynthDef::, or a link::Classes/MIDIEndPoint::.
argument:: format
Mono or stereo sound.

SUBSECTION:: Discussion

code::
// boot up slice
l = SLiCE();

// add a folder of soundfiles (if name is nil then the file name will be used)
l.addSound(nil, "/path/to/folder/");

// add a single sample
l.addSound(\kick, "/path/to/folder/909kick3.aif");

// add a synth function
l.addSound(\blip, {|freq|
	var sig;
	sig = Blip.ar(blip, \numHarm.kr(9));
});

p = Pbind(
	\sound, Prand([\kick, \blip]),
	\numHarm, Pwhite(0, 10)
).play;
::

METHOD:: master
Set parameters on the master synth.
argument:: par
The parameter to set.
argument:: val
The value to set it to.

Available parameters are:
code::
\revTime // reverb time in seconds (0.1 - inf)
\saturation // tanh distortion added to the final mix (1 - 99)
::

METHOD:: bpm
Set the tempo in BPM.

METHOD:: listSounds
Lists the currently loaded sounds by name.

METHOD:: listParams
Lists the currently available parameter space. ToDo!

METHOD:: setServerOptions
argument:: aServerOptions
Private method used for setting good limits for link::Classes/ServerOptions::. The following values are set:

code::
memSize = 2097152;
numBuffers = 8192;
numWireBufs = 32768;
maxSynthDefs = 8192;
numAudioBusChannels = 8192;
numControlBusChannels = 131072;
safetyClipThreshold = 1.0;
o.loadDefs = false;
::

METHOD:: init

EXAMPLES::

code::
l = SLiCE(); // enter SLiCE

(
l.bpm(72); // set the tempo in beats per minute
l.master(\revTime, 3); // set the reverb decay time (0.1 - inf)
l.master(\saturation, 4); // set the saturation amount (1 - 99)

Pdef(\a,
	Pbind(
		\sound, \sine,
		\ctranspose, Prand([0, -12, 12], inf),
		\note, Prand([0, 3, 5, 8, 10], inf),
		\rel, 3,
		\atk, 0.66,
		\tremolo, 0.5,
		\tremoloRate, Pwhite(1, 8),
		\shaper, 1.0,
		\shaperBufA, 1,
		\shaperBufB, Pwhite(0, 7),
		\shaperMorph, Ndef(\morph, {SinOsc.ar(0.9)}),
		\shaperWarp, Pmeanrand(1.0, 8.0),
		\delay, 0.2,
		\reverb, 0.3,
		\amp, Pseq([0.2, 0.15, 0.1] * 0.8, inf),
		\dur, 0.25,
		\prob, 0.4
	)
).play;
)

Pdef(\a).stop;
::
